{"Backup codes are generated as lowercase hex, but login and disable flows compare user-supplied backup code without normalizing case, so uppercase input will always be rejected as IncorrectBackupCode": 0.9362280368804932, "In disable.ts, a backup code is validated via indexOf but never consumed/invalidated before the final prisma.user.update, allowing two concurrent disable requests with the same valid backup code to both pass validation (race condition)": 0.5566441416740417, "In disable.ts, the backup code path uses throw new Error(ErrorCode.InternalServerError) for missing encryption key case, producing a raw 500 error without JSON body, but client-side expects body.error in JSON response": 0.7479640245437622, "The backup-codes copy button always shows a success toast even if navigator.clipboard.writeText fails, since the Promise is neither awaited nor caught": 0.9777370095252991, "Backup codes are generated and persisted to database in setup.ts before TOTP verification is complete, so if user abandons setup after password step, codes are stored but never displayed to user": 0.7720238566398621, "EnableTwoFactorModal creates a Blob object URL for backup code download but does not revoke it when the modal is closed/reset, leaving the URL allocated for the lifetime of the page": 0.8270948529243469}